<article class="env-definition" id="04IP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04IP">Definition <span data-tag="04IP">7.30.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf on $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The topos $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{F}$ is called the <em>localization of the topos $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ at $\mathcal{F}$</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The morphism of topoi $j_\mathcal {F} : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{F} \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/04GZ" data-tag="04GZ">7.30.1</a> is called the <em>localization morphism</em>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>